                "retweet_count": 4,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "The phase-out of the R&D Tax Credit is hitting small businesses hard, particularly those in the medical field dedicated to creating breakthrough medicines. Developing new treatments already carries a substantial price tag. Losing the ability to fully deduct their research expenses only adds more hurdles and red tape, which further strains small businesses and potentially impedes patient access to new medications and medical equipment.\n\nDuring today\u2019s @HouseSmallBiz hearing, we discussed how increased taxes and regulations have placed burdens on small businesses seeking to provide quality healthcare and treatments to their patients.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1715188974,
                "view_count": 615
