                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Earlier today, I attended the ribbon-cutting ceremony at the Wyoming County Healthcare Center, formerly Tyler Memorial Hospital. With Guthrie now providing medical services and a full-time ambulance service, the center is fully operational, restoring vital healthcare access to Wyoming County. Thanks to Bill Ruark and his family, who purchased and revitalized the property, the Wyoming County Healthcare Center is paving the way for more accessible healthcare in the region. Supported by a $213,000 Appalachian Regional Commission (ARC) grant my office helped secure, as well as contributions from the Neighborhood Assistance Program (NAP), and the AllOne Foundation, the center is now ready to meet the healthcare needs of Wyoming County.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1727984397,
                "view_count": 426
